Z||000000||mrgone||07-25-2001||10:00 PM||||name the movie based on some vague description.<P>these movies i have seen once about 13 years ago<P>ok this one i know, can you guess it.<P>Pink lambo countache (i think it was pink), mid 80's movie, i think it had john candy in a vw jetta...<BR>big car chase scene with lambo. <BR>lambo burns down a dirt road. cop says "i hope he brought his water wings"  Scene changes to granpa teaching granson how to skip rocks on a pond "the key is the rock has to be perfectley flat"<BR>The lambo then skips across the water doing about mach 4.<P>guess it i loved that movie<P>ok now these i dont know the names of<P>movie about stealing cars, had a car auction in it, licence plates of a car (virginia plates i think) 00GAL they would steal cars and strip them vins and all and hide the car in a garage. had a wicked ending where guy is driving a sweet red and white muscle car, smashes it up real good, loses the cops for a few minutes, goes into a car wash where the exact same car is just coming out "lady, we washed your car incorrectly, if you would please give the keys we would run it through for free"   then he runs the smashed up car through and drives the good one away.<P>i saw this and the first one when i was about 7 or 8 years old. im 19 now, pretty good memory eh? only when it comes to cars.. if only i was interested in anything else.<P>and i keep hearing that the gone in 60 seconds isnt the original?? ive asked at blockbuster they dont know. what is the name of it???||||reg||1
Z||000001||California Kid||07-25-2001||10:32 PM||||Sounds like your talking about a couple movies. Looks like you're after:<P>Original Movie "Gone in 60 Seconds", main feature car is Mustang Mach. I think the code name used for the Mustang in the movie was "elenor".<P>Seems you have a piece of "Vanishing Point" in there. Pretty good movie about a guy making a bet to deliver a car across country in impossible hours. Feature Car was a white 70-71 Cuda/Challenger (big block or Hemi), moved out pretty good.<P>Here's another real old classic for ya "California Kid" with Martin Sheen. He gets even with a small town "hot shot" sheriff (souped up squad car), by dialing in his hot rod roadster.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000002||West Coast Fiero||07-25-2001||10:39 PM||||first one was Cannon Ball Run, the second was either Bullett or Gone in 60 Seconds (original)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Slammed Fiero||07-25-2001||10:45 PM||||No it's not Cannonball run.<P>Speed Zone (1989) <P>Part of a red Lambo on the box<P>the 2nd one Couldn't possibly be Bullit , wrong story all together. Frank Bullit plays a Cop , someone in a safehouse gets murdered. Won an Oscar for film editing in 1968<P>2nd one is original gone in 60 seconds, which differs a lot from the one that just came out. Intrestingly enough the one that came out differs a lot from the script that was originally written. Nicholas cage was suppose to drive a GT-40 , not a mustang. Was deemed too expensive to wreck GT-40's at 150 grand a pop for repro's<P>Enjoy<P>JM <p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 07-25-2001).]||||reg||1
