Z||000012||fierohoho||07-26-2001||09:33 AM||||Original movie "Gone in 60 seconds" stared Ron "Opie" Howard.<P>Vanishing Point, bought it a while back, one thing to say about it, AWESOME!, 60's, drugs, muscle cars and a naked blonde on a motorcycle in the desert.<P>Stared Barry Neuman and Clevon Little as the blind DJ.<P>As I recall it had a pretty surealistic ending. A definate mindblower of a movie.<P>Slammed Fiero, is the new version of Vanishing Point out on video or was it a TV release?<P>For the younger guys who don't remember, the "Cannonball Run" movie was based on an actual race written up I believe in an issue of Hot Rod magazine, the reason for the race was to prove you could drive coast to coast at high speed safely.<P>Anyone know for sure which issue or mag the article was in? I wouldn't mind reading it again as it was a hoot.(thats small town talk for funny) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000013||Dave Gunsul||07-26-2001||12:03 PM||||Actually, the original Gone in 60 Sec's stared H.B. Halicki.<BR>"Opie" starred in two old car movies called;<BR>Eat My Dust and Grand Theft Auto.<BR>I don't have these because they were really horrible movies.<P>I actually forgot some tapes in my collection.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>The Driver  (this is a movie about a getaway driver)<BR>The Motor Week video about the Fiero<BR>The local T.V. show that did an hour long show from V8 Archies.<BR>V8 Archies swap tape. (i've watched this more than Archie has  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>The Home Improvement episode about Tims first car which was a Corvair.<BR>Return To Macon County. (this was a bomb.)<BR>The Story of Camaro.<BR>Actual footage of Bob Bondarant (sp?) driving a real Corvette Grand Sport. This is<BR>the real Grand Sport too not that crappy purple thing with the white stripe! <P>Would like to have: <BR>Knight Rider episode about the car gang.<BR>21 Jumpstreet episode about the street racers.<BR>A movie called Corvette Summer starring Mark,<BR>"Luke Skywalker", Hamill.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||4
