Z||000019||Raydar||07-27-2001||10:48 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierohoho:<BR><B>...For the younger guys who don't remember, the "Cannonball Run" movie was based on an actual race written up I believe in an issue of Hot Rod magazine, the reason for the race was to prove you could drive coast to coast at high speed safely.<P>Anyone know for sure which issue or mag the article was in? I wouldn't mind reading it again as it was a hoot.(thats small town talk for funny)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Car and Driver was an "unofficial" sponsor of the Cannonball, which was officially known as "The Cannonball Baker Sea To Shining Sea Memorial Trophy Dash". One of the main instigators was one of their journalists, Brock Yates (who drove a nicely warmed-over 72 Challenger in the race.)<BR>Seems like it only happened for a few years. After that, it became too well-known and too "hot".<P>Yates and C&D still sponsor "One Lap Of America". They organize a huge tour/rally, and (supposedly) only flog their cars on racetrack venues. <P><BR>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 07-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||Raydar||07-27-2001||10:53 AM||||The Cannonball was in August 1975 Car and Driver. <BR>Here's a reprint... <A HREF="http://www.onelapofamerica.com/Cannonball/stories/1975.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.onelapofamerica.com/Cannonball/stories/1975.htm</A> <P>Do a web search of "Cannonball Baker"<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000021||Slammed Fiero||07-27-2001||10:56 AM||||I know three guys that run the one lap , most notibly Dan Corcran and Rick potter, Rick has the yellow RX7 , you can see it in Car and driver he won ssgt1 this year.<P>In anycase it's still pretty open on the roads. I know Dan corcran has been arrested, a lot of them have police scanners in the car. Rick has gotten numerous tickets.<P>The truck was loaned to a friend (Marc Guimont) he won the Suv class with it in 1999 , 350hp V6 awd <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stevecar.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Reg5.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/s10_1.jpg"> <P>The firebird has a 383Supercharged Lt1 pushes 580 RWHP , The RX7 is a mid 11 sec car built by Pete Farell Supercars , uses a single turbo<P>The guy with the white firebird ran the original cannonball back in the day , he still wears the jacket..I want the jacket (haah)<P>JM <BR>||||reg||1
